# macro_expand.tkr — the §14 A3 ACCEPT host: Family-A `@macro(...)` expansion. Each scenario names
# itself and asserts its announced value through `run` in `main.tks`, so a relapse names itself. A
# `@macro` call is rewritten pre-type-check into its `lowering { … }` fragment with `${}` holes filled
# by the caller's arguments; nested macro calls expand to a bounded fixpoint.

Feature: macro_expand — Family-A macro expansion (§14 A3)

  Scenario: macro_twice — @twice(5) splices its arg twice: (5) + (5) = 10
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario macro_twice: ok"

  Scenario: macro_sum3 — @sum3(1, 2, 3) splices three args: (1)+(2)+(3) = 6
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario macro_sum3: ok"

  Scenario: macro_quad_nested — @quad(5) expands through @twice twice: ((5)+(5))+((5)+(5)) = 20
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario macro_quad_nested: ok"
